<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish govt sets Oct 29 as date for 1998 budget.</title>
<headline>Irish govt sets Oct 29 as date for 1998 budget.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The date of the 1998 budget has been fixed for October 29, the Irish government announced after a cabinet meeting on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The budget, the first to be held in the autumn, brings Ireland into line with other European Union countries.</p>
<p>Finance minister Ruairi Quinn unveiled his 1997 budget in January.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
